Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.34 phase 3: the whole bag in the equip list, move an item between Digimon

P6.34 phase 3 (docs/P6.34_MENU_FLOW.md section 14, P6.33 owner decisions 2 and 3;
orchestrator defaults pending owner confirmation). In Status > Equipment's item
list (STSTATUS_chooseEquipItem, equip_panel.c) Square cycles a filter when the key
items_bag_view is on (default 1; DW3_ITEMS_BAG_VIEW=0 or the file key 0 is the
original list and Square does nothing):

* 0 this slot: the original list;
* 1 all weapons, 2 all armor and accessories: the whole bag from
  ITEM_FUNCS.list 2 / 3 + 4, the items that fit the slot first, the others after
  (grey, Cross does nothing, as in the original);
* 3 worn by others: one row per item the other party members wear that fits the
  slot (and STSTATUS_canEquip says this partner can wear), the count column shows
  the copies they wear, and the line under the help text names the wearer.
  Cross takes the item from its wearer with STSTATUS_equip(wearer, slot, 0) and
  puts it on this partner with STSTATUS_equip, the only writer; the phase 2
  return to the slot list follows.

The list title shows the filter name and the row count (port strings in
port/items_menu, EN FR DE IT ES); the cursor goes to "none", the stat preview to
the emptied slot, the scroll bar is rebuilt for the new count. The filter resets
to 0 each time the list opens from the slot list. Square is not used by the
Status screens in the original game.

Logs (port/items_menu): "dw3-items-menu: bag-view filter=.. slot=.. rows=..
worn-elsewhere=.." and "move item=.. from=.. from-slot=.. to=.. slot=.. bag=a->b
worn=a->b".

